==Rules==
{{ColosseumRule|Uber Clearance|1}}

==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 8 seconds<sup>240f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Tackey]] spawns after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Casaurian Darkjo]] spawns as the boss.
**1 [[Tackey]] spawns.
**5 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**1 [[Midnite D.]] spawns after 63.33 seconds<sup>1,900f</sup>.
**2 [[Fallen Bear]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 33.33~36.67 seconds<sup>1,000f~1,100f</sup>.
**5 [[Kroxo]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
**2 [[Scissoroo]]s spawn after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**1 [[Mesocosmocyclone]] spawns after 133.33 seconds<sup>4,000f</sup>.

==Strategy==
While this stage might look a bit easy given that it's on base hit, do not let that fool you as hitting the base prematurely will have you be greeted by a Darkjo, two Tackeys, a Midnite D. and two Fallen Bears. Because of this, abuse the fact that this is on base hit as much as you can by taking it slow and farming cash off of the Doge Darks, as well as eliminating the Tackey. The Mesocosmocyclone is balanced around CotC 3 completion, but it shouldn't be an issue as most strategies focus on destroying the base before it spawns.

Since the all the nasty stuff takes over a minute to spawn after you hit the base, your main goal is rushing the Darkjo as fast as you can. Your main units to help you do so will probably be a Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]] or a high levelled [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]], alongside [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Make sure that Bahamut is the one to hit the base to get his full damage off on the Tackey and Darkjo. Alongside units like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] to clear out the peons, Darkjo should die before the Akus spawn and you should have free reign to beat up the base. To minimize the threat of the Akus here, run a Shield Piercer like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] or [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]] to break their Shields and force damage knockbacks on the Akus.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*Anti-Dark nukers like [[Adventurer Kanna (Uber Rare Cat)|Adventurer Kanna]], [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Shingen]] or [[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Jizo's Moving Castle]] are excellent here to take care of the Darkjo. Bonus points if they have Behemoth Slayer (like Kanna) or also target Aku (like [[Amakusa Shiro (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Amakusa]].

